    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="05652083-5b4f-5980-a72f-7ffc61ba894d" activityNameId="a3d7ccac-71e8-59c5-a69e-e26e09255c4b" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Asphalt concrete (AC) foundation layer, 80% recycling, high temperature, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Asphalt concrete (AC) foundation layer, 80% recycling, high temperature, at plant
Modern Swiss technologies for regional storage facilities, material extraction, and asphalt production. Based on survey data from 73 asphalt mixing plants. 
UUID: 37020686-8fdd-47d3-abfd-8f918172d2b0
This dataset covers the production of average Asphalt Concrete (AC F) foundation layers in Switzerland, with 80% reclaimed asphalt. The process represents an average AC F, derived from the mean material composition of AC F 16, AC F 22 and AC F 32 layers. It includes raw material extraction, transportation, and manufacturing processes.
Location: Switzerland
Technology: Production of hot mix asphalt concrete AC F, using industrial machinery.
Time period: Review of data currency scheduled after 5 years.
Production volume: 351352456 t 
Sampling: Survey
Extrapolations: None
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_37020686-8fdd-47d3-abfd-8f918172d2b0.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
